From 69485303ab57737987b0f6648098e0136e83ab62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Marcelo Poblete (via Claude)" <marcelopoblete.us@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 00:15:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Conduit module gets Overview -> Map -> Equipment
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Second module in the common shape. Conduit had two tables and no map
at all.

- ConduitMapCanvas.tsx (new): Ductería's own map — civil structures as
  markers and duct runs as lines, and nothing else. Not the combined
  project map and not the fiber one: per
  claude/plan-separacion-modulos.md this module draws civil works only.
  New work is solid, existing reused duct is dashed and grey, matching
  how a plan separates proposed from as-built, and that split is also
  what decides whether the item is billed.
- A run has no geometry of its own — it mirrors a fiber route — so the
  line is drawn from that route's segments rather than duplicating the
  trace. getConduitData now returns those segments.
- ConduitPageClient: Overview | Map | Equipment tabs. Overview is the
  metrics banner; Equipment keeps the existing Runs/Structures tables
  and the cross-section panel. Selection is shared across Map and
  Equipment, so picking a structure in the table centres it on the map
  and its cross-section stays open.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ScqTACWd5u51GDZPenDDdM
